---
const repo = "https://git.gentoo.party/sam/irchad-ng";
const site = "https://irchad.chat/";
const title = "Terms of Service · IrChad";
const description = "The rules for using the IrChad apps and the official IrChad network, in plain language.";
const effective = "15 November 2026";
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <title>{title}</title>
  <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
  <meta name="description" content={description} />
  <link rel="canonical" href={`${site}terms`} />
</head>
<body>
  <main>
    <p><a href="/">← IrChad</a></p>
    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="muted">Effective {effective}. By using the IrChad apps or the official IrChad network, you agree to these terms.</p>

    <h2>What these terms cover</h2>
    <p>These terms cover the IrChad apps for Android, iOS, Linux and Windows, and the official network that IrChad's developer runs, which is linked from this site.
      Anyone can run their own IrChad network. Each of those networks is run by its own operator, and that operator's rules apply there instead of the network rules below.</p>

    <h2>The software</h2>
    <p>IrChad is free and open source software, licensed under the <a href="https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.html">GNU General Public License, version 3 or later</a>.
      That license governs what you can do with the code, and nothing in these terms limits the rights it gives you. The source is on <a href={repo}>our Git server</a>.</p>

    <h2>Your account</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>You must be at least 13 years old, or older if your country requires it, to make an account.</li>
      <li>Keep your password safe. You're responsible for what's posted from your account.</li>
      <li>If you sign in with Discord, Discord's <a href="https://discord.com/terms">Terms of Service</a> also apply to that sign-in.
        We receive only your Discord user ID and username, which we use to link the sign-in to your account. See the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Acceptable use on the official network</h2>
    <p>Don't use the official network to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>post or share anything illegal, including any content that sexually exploits children;</li>
      <li>harass, threaten or dox other people, or impersonate them;</li>
      <li>send spam or malware, or run phishing or scams;</li>
      <li>attack, overload or disrupt the service, including flooding, mass scraping, or getting around bans and limits;</li>
      <li>infringe other people's copyright or other rights.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Channel operators can moderate their own channels. The network operator may remove content, and suspend or delete accounts that break these rules, with or without notice.
      Where the law requires it, we may report illegal content to the authorities.</p>

    <h2>Your content</h2>
    <p>You keep ownership of what you post. To run the service, you give the network permission to store, copy and deliver it to the people and devices it's meant for.
      That includes keeping channel history and serving the files you upload. Anyone with a file's link can open it, so don't upload anything you wouldn't share.
      Channels are also visible to people using ordinary IRC clients, which may keep their own copies.</p>

    <h2>Other services</h2>
    <p>Some features rely on other services, and their own terms apply: <a href="https://klipy.com">KLIPY</a> for GIF search, the UnifiedPush app you pick for push notifications on Android, and Discord if you sign in with it.</p>

    <h2>No warranty</h2>
    <p>IrChad and the official network are provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, just as the GPL says for the code.
      We don't promise that the service will be available, uninterrupted or free of bugs. We may change or shut down the service at any time.
      To the extent the law allows, IrChad's developer isn't liable for any loss or damage that comes from using the apps or the network, including lost messages or data.</p>

    <h2>Ending your use</h2>
    <p>You can stop using IrChad and <a href="/delete-account">delete your account</a> at any time.
      We may suspend or end your access to the official network if you break these terms.</p>

    <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>If these terms change, we'll update the effective date above and mention significant changes in the release notes. If you keep using IrChad after a change, you accept the new terms.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Email <a href="mailto:android@irchad.chat">android@irchad.chat</a>, or open an issue on the <a href={`${repo}/issues`}>issue tracker</a>.</p>
  </main>
</body>
</html>

<style is:global>
  /* The same Catppuccin tokens as privacy.astro. */
  :root { color-scheme: light dark; --bg: #e6e9ef; --fg: #4c4f69; --muted: #6c6f85; --accent: #40a02b; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { :root { --bg: #11111b; --fg: #cdd6f4; --muted: #a6adc8; --accent: #a6e3a1; } }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { margin: 0; background: var(--bg); color: var(--fg); font: 16px/1.6 system-ui, sans-serif; }
  main { max-width: 44rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 16px 4rem; }
  a { color: inherit; text-decoration-color: var(--accent); }
  a:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 2px; }
  h1 { font-size: 2.25rem; margin: 1rem 0 0; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.3rem; margin: 2.5rem 0 .5rem; }
  .muted { color: var(--muted); }
  li { margin: .35rem 0; }
</style>
